 "subject": "Java edge accuracy: bytecode oracle, overload narrowing, native retirement",
 "body": "Oracle (--lang java): javac -g + javap parsing \u2014 invoke* instructions,\nLineNumberTables, arity-resolved overloads; JDK-only, no deps. Pin:\ncommons-lang, the overload stress test.\n\nThree fixes from the first measurement (P 0.146!):\n- retired the native Java text-matching call edges (edged every overload\n  of every name seen: 22k edges vs oracle's 3.8k); native keeps\n  inheritance + uses-type, the graph layer owns calls\n- arity narrowing from astkit v0.4.7 Argc; argument-type conflict\n  rejection from v0.4.8 Args (varargs/type-vars/widening supertypes are\n  neutral, only conflicts drop)\n- javaLocalTypes (params, fields incl ancestors, typed locals), Java\n  same-package scope, extends-based inheritance reuse\n\ncommons-lang: P 0.146 -> 0.455, F1 0.249 -> 0.553, universe 96.6%.\nGate live with minUniverse grammar-drift canary (now on all entries).\nGo/Python/TS byte-identical.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
